  "reason": "The paper code moved from 277-281mm down to 288-292mm: its strip is now RESERVED by a running tfoot rather than shared with the body (#1958). Both copies are recorded by this run. The MARKING KEY is the one that matters here: while the code was still the table cell's last child, the last block's invisible trailing margin pushed the reservation past the page and gave the key a second sheet carrying nothing but the code - content ended at 278.5mm, comfortably inside the 281mm limit. Moving the code outside the table and zeroing that margin restored it to one page, which is what is being recorded; the key's last body ink is 278.54mm, within a pixel of the limit. Anchors unchanged in both copies, 156 connected pixels each. No DOCX baseline is affected.",
